    "title": "Hugh Jackman Gets Support from Girlfriend Sutton Foster at 'The Death of Robin Hood' World Premiere in NYC - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Tommy Pisani ,\n2 hours ago\nHugh Jackman is hitting the red carpet with girlfriend Sutton Foster at the premiere of his new movie!\nThe two Tony winners posed for photos together at the world premiere of The Death of Robin Hood on Wednesday evening (June 10) held at AMC Lincoln Square 13 in New York City.\nFor the event, Hugh , 57, looked sharp in a gray suit and black button-down shirt while Sutton , 51, wore a navy dress.\nAlso joining Hugh at the premiere were his co-stars Jodie Comer , Bill Skarsgard , Murray Bartlett , and Faith Delaney along with writer/director Michael Sarnoski .\nHere’s the logline: Grappling with his past after a life of crime and murder, Robin Hood finds himself gravely injured after a battle he thought would be his last. In the hands of a mysterious woman, he is offered a chance at salvation.\nThe Death of Robin Hood hits theaters on June 19. Watch the trailer here !\nFYI: Hugh is wearing a Brioni suit, John Lobb shoes and a vintage Rolex watch from Iconic Timepieces . Sutton is wearing a Marina Moscone dress, Manolo Blahnik shoes, and vintage Grown Brilliance while carrying a Judith Leiber bag. Jodie is wearing a Jessica McCormack ring.\nBrowse through the gallery below for more photos from the premiere…\nThe post appeared first on .\n2",
    "summary": "The two Tony winners posed for photos together at the world premiere of The Death of Robin Hood on Wednesday evening (June 10) held at AMC Lincoln Square 13 in New York City. For the event, Hugh , 57, looked sharp in a gray suit and black button-down shirt while Sutton , 51, wore a navy dress. Also joining Hugh at the premiere were his co-stars Jodie Comer , Bill Skarsgard , Murray Bartlett , and Faith Delaney along with writer/director Michael Sarnoski .",
